BentoPDF 2.8.10 — reference distribution

Upstream: https://github.com/alam00000/bentopdf/releases/tag/v2.8.10
License: AGPL-3.0-only (full text in LICENSE). During environment/build.sh,
environment/fetch.py downloads the full upstream source, including its LICENSE
and build scripts, as solution/bentopdf-2.8.10-source.tar.gz. SOURCE.json pins
the download URL and SHA-256. The installer retains this archive and the PDF
viewer source archive under /app/solution in the final reference image.
No product source code is changed. The offline build uses the documented
Simple deployment and local asset configuration. The task-authored server.py,
start.sh and solve.sh are provided under the Apache License 2.0, the license
of the Program Bench Pro repository.

Rebuilding the included site

Extract the source archive, install Node.js 22.21.1, and run npm ci with the
included package-lock.json. Run npm run build with these environment variables:

SIMPLE_MODE=true
DISABLE_GITHUB_STARS=true
COMPRESSION_MODE=o
VITE_EMBEDPDF_FONTS_URL=/fonts/embedpdf
VITE_WASM_PYMUPDF_URL=/wasm/pymupdf/
VITE_WASM_GS_URL=/wasm/gs/assets/
VITE_WASM_CPDF_URL=/wasm/cpdf/dist/
VITE_TESSERACT_WORKER_URL=/wasm/ocr/worker.min.js
VITE_TESSERACT_CORE_URL=/wasm/ocr/core
VITE_TESSERACT_LANG_URL=/wasm/ocr/lang-data
VITE_TESSERACT_AVAILABLE_LANGUAGES=eng
VITE_OCR_FONT_BASE_URL=/wasm/ocr/fonts

Stage these unmodified npm packages into dist/wasm: coherentpdf at cpdf/ and
Tesseract's worker.min.js at ocr/ with its core package at ocr/core/, which are
listed in SOURCE.json, and @bentopdf/pymupdf-wasm 0.11.16 (PyMuPDF) at
pymupdf/ and @bentopdf/gs-wasm 0.1.1 (Ghostscript) at gs/, whose package
manifests, licenses and source references are in LICENSES/processing/
(pymupdf-wasm/, ghostscript-wasm/ and source-availability.md). Place the
English traineddata file under ocr/lang-data/ and NotoSans-Regular.ttf under
ocr/fonts/.
The upstream source already includes the LibreOffice WASM files. The shipped
ZIP uses these files verbatim, excluding source maps, Brotli duplicates and
build-only scripts. It is served with the static allowlist and CSP in server.py.

Third-party software

LICENSES/dependencies/ preserves the license/notice files of npm dependencies;
LICENSES/dependencies.json records their versions, licenses and upstream source
repositories. LICENSES/processing/ includes notices and source instructions for
separately packaged processing engines. All associated notices are part of the
reference distribution; they are not served through the black-box observation surface.
The installed reference image retains the downloaded source alongside the binaries.
No proprietary or commercial-only implementation is used.

Archive packaging

The locally assembled site is stored in numbered .chunk001, .chunk002, ...
files of at most 48,000,000 bytes. solve.sh concatenates them in lexical
order into bentopdf-2.8.10-offline.zip. The static server reads that ZIP
without extracting it. Product assets are unchanged by this packaging.

The complete upstream release source is downloaded from
https://api.github.com/repos/alam00000/bentopdf/tarball/v2.8.10
as bentopdf-2.8.10-source.tar.gz. The corresponding PDF viewer fork source is
https://api.github.com/repos/alam00000/bentopdf-pdfium-viewer/tarball/051abe5b72a9
as bentopdf-viewer-source-051abe5b72a9.tar.gz. SOURCE.json pins both archive
hashes. environment/fetch.py retrieves both archives before the image build;
solution/solve.sh copies them and the license notices into /app/solution.
environment/Dockerfile.reference retains that directory in the final reference
image. The offline-build inputs and configuration are documented above and in
SOURCE.json; third-party processing sources are listed in LICENSES/processing/.
